{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7e1a2c4-0000-4a2b-9c3d-collectionsworkflow",
    "name": "ERP Collection Reporting Workflow",
    "description": "Full API flow for the collections service: upload a workbook, watch the pipeline run (load -> validate -> explain -> calculate -> control gate -> summarise -> persist), then read every output.\n\n## How to use this\n\n1. Import both environment files too (`local.postman_environment.json` for the Docker-served app on this machine, `ngrok.postman_environment.json` for the public tunnel).\n2. Select the **Collections Workflow - Local** environment (top-right dropdown).\n3. Run **Runs > Create Run - Dataset A (Blocks)** first -- its test script saves the returned run's id into `{{blocked_run_id}}` and `{{run_id}}` automatically. Every other request in this collection reads `{{run_id}}`, so just re-run whichever \"Create Run\" request you want to inspect next and everything downstream follows it.\n4. Then work through **Reports** top to bottom against that run.\n5. Run **Create Run - Dataset B (Passes)** to see the other outcome (`{{passed_run_id}}` is saved separately so you can compare both without re-uploading).\n\n## The one manual step Postman won't let you script\n\nPostman (desktop, v10+) strips the `src` path out of file-type form-data fields on import, for security -- it will not silently read a local file path from a JSON someone sent you. Each \"Create Run\" request below already has the field ready named `file`; you only need to click into the Body tab and select the file once per request:\n\n- Dataset A (blocks): `{{dataset_a_path}}`\n- Dataset B (passes): `{{dataset_b_path}}`\n- Or your own file: any `.xlsx` with the same four sheets (Customers, Invoices, Payments, Region_Mapping)\n\nAfter you select it once, Postman remembers it for that request going forward.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:8000" },
    { "key": "run_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "blocked_run_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "passed_run_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "dataset_a_path", "value": "" },
    { "key": "dataset_b_path", "value": "" },
    { "key": "corrupt_path", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
